  "max_abs_kill_difference_across_variants": 0.31036579421114796,
  "interpretation": "The ordinal claim -- PBP-3 agent costs several-fold more danger signal at matched exposure, while killing within about 0.1 log10 -- is reproduced under the bacterial-layer refit, under the fitted kill rate alone, under a kill_C50 corrected to the calibration isolate's measured MIC, and under three immune structures spanning no immune killing to a sustained effector pool. What the refit moves is the dose scale, not the comparison: because matching is done at equal %fT>MIC, a change in the effective MIC multiplies both agents' doses by the same factor (x1.85 to x2.31 here, exactly the MIC ratio), so the cost ratio and the kill difference under a pure kill_C50 correction are unchanged to the last digit. The residual kill difference is the one quantity that is NOT robust: it is 0.105 log10 at the refit optimum and 0.232 with the Hill exponent held at 4, and the data cannot distinguish those two exponents. The defaults are unchanged; adopting the refit is the author's decision. See scripts/ds_bacterial_refit.py and the Limitations."
 },
